{"objects":[{"id":"flow","instance":"instance--b96dad5f-c519-5a1f-a718-912ca4a86c02","objects":["attack-action--1","attack-action--2","attack-action--3","attack-action--4","attack-action--5","attack-action--6","attack-action--7","attack-condition--1","email-message--1","file--1","email-message--2","instance--3536a568-610f-5570-bba9-6dfe97bc9c2e","instance--384798bd-a84b-5feb-8d38-7f9d0a087f11","instance--057c9c6b-5f9d-5a42-a700-338d5f0eb74a","instance--7e8c9301-c3f8-55e9-8894-e81f1b6203d9","instance--b6d82c28-0a68-5c6f-b058-c1e072f51852","instance--3622ace1-abf1-5f6e-a5de-a6f584dc1f66","instance--5824580a-ff0f-5565-bba6-97a7c9ed3a5e","instance--cb38395e-f726-5a39-90a8-2999c2025a1d","instance--d0f200db-7b2a-50a9-9430-330537193c08","instance--573cfe4e-db2c-5dae-9d0d-40adc6ec7a73"],"properties":[["name","FIN7 fileless spearphishing and DDE-based infection flow"],["description","CyberScoop article describing FIN7 spear-phishing lures, Microsoft Office attachment abuse, DDE-based execution, and fileless code injection into memory."],["scope","campaign"],["author",[["name","Unknown"]]],["external_references",[["item-1",[["source_name","www.cyberscoop.com"],["url","https://www.cyberscoop.com/fin7-dde-morphisec-fileless-malware/"]]]]]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--ad592d05-6969-5b51-98a8-1ad9b6aab896","120":"instance--5850a8f4-8241-5e73-9bf0-dcd376cd5025","150":"instance--0da1498f-3beb-5916-a249-e0410a4a81e4","180":"instance--d3632784-7391-5a29-83e2-edab51db56c6","210":"instance--8bc47ca5-ca73-5a04-a9ea-918608f10871","240":"instance--6546eef6-c5ad-516e-a417-89916e651648","270":"instance--244e5a69-f465-564e-9d2c-93d4da44fc57","30":"instance--6a1fca3c-fdb6-536a-bbea-61ac2349a700","300":"instance--043a5b44-2864-5565-abce-1909204e5485","330":"instance--e10eb918-2b0b-56f4-9c82-f345ce21276c","60":"instance--33a99d1b-dad8-51f6-be74-e1614db9151b","90":"instance--380c79e9-b1eb-547c-bf01-a011db1201c1"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--1","properties":[["name","Spearphish targets with malicious attachments"],["description","The lures rely on social engineering \u2014 Microsoft users will generally get a pop-up box asking them if they want to \u201cenable content\u201d or \u201cupdate links\u201d in the document they\u2019re opening \u2014 and are typically spear-phished very carefully at a small number of targets."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0001","technique":"T1566.001"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--4f4d03a8-4502-5010-997b-9943e254395b","120":"instance--cefe62ac-5b6e-5ead-84fc-b4c632913a73","150":"instance--4d07a740-2467-5b95-ac8d-4a2ee8edd11e","180":"instance--1205f03c-a457-5a0b-87ef-3bbb7aac110f","210":"instance--96e7dc6a-9f86-5f69-8d45-a566303cd4c0","240":"instance--66237af6-bb19-5a51-9fa2-cbc4a96186f5","270":"instance--836dfd42-b475-50ca-9acf-4f11bd32b89f","30":"instance--efe92997-cc5c-538a-90bc-c09ffb1379f4","300":"instance--9c4a24ae-1426-5cb5-9d7c-792e6dd325b7","330":"instance--06c6a74a-ca7d-5703-88ea-a06a0933d21a","60":"instance--5e4f84e5-56b7-5b8f-9bc3-b4d59d371123","90":"instance--019deb6a-bab3-57db-9a53-11e3564bf7a4"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--2","properties":[["name","Send SEC spoofed Word lure"],["description","Earlier this year, FIN7 was suspected of being behind that used emails appearing to come from the SEC\u2019s Electronic Data Gathering, Analysis and Retrieval (EDGAR) online filing system. The emails bore a Microsoft Word attachment titled \u201cImportant changes to form 10K.\u201d"],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0001","technique":"T1566.001"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--0ce35aea-35a2-52ae-a67b-985306bdefe7","120":"instance--312639d5-e6d9-57b1-850d-28f0a1eac2f6","150":"instance--9551a25e-2558-512e-9894-dd64a8d662bf","180":"instance--403becce-e0ad-5dcd-bc14-7c00453907da","210":"instance--2305f501-2712-5ec6-9d4e-1371b011e937","240":"instance--cf1b8cf6-1cbd-5afb-b653-aa693889dab5","270":"instance--1d3dc59a-40a0-5670-aa3e-1304ff762003","30":"instance--77063d4f-503a-5e9b-b622-15aa2cc6a8e7","300":"instance--beaab67f-8a54-5982-8c5d-9d2ed2d42c9f","330":"instance--4d3274ff-ef14-5a53-99be-01575194a98e","60":"instance--4154a6bf-290b-5fce-a557-5dc0f3e700fb","90":"instance--2992bc0b-df57-54e5-a17b-03a964338c09"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--3","properties":[["name","Spoof SEC address with DDE attachment"],["description","Last week, researchers at Cisco Talos spear-phishing emails, with a similarly spoofed SEC address, bearing an attachment that used DDE to launch a \u201ccomplex multi-stage infection process,\u201d typical of FIN7."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0001","technique":"T1566.001"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--0f6e4da7-a5f4-54d7-866f-3bc6e8bcb019","120":"instance--015254b5-0906-577e-b3e3-3899f837d118","150":"instance--f7af5b8c-330a-58d5-b0da-a3d5f0bc6ad0","180":"instance--9f27ab21-2382-567d-b022-74ad5a29bd08","210":"instance--d799eb0a-7600-5b1a-a298-c47a78ceae4b","240":"instance--911c2c52-5974-5e08-b0b6-a9084d57c6ee","270":"instance--286444b4-97a1-58cd-9ca3-cffa04a15351","30":"instance--92192c38-5143-50e0-8c39-a96ea86e32e2","300":"instance--82bb3de0-bea5-5651-a1de-583283258c6d","330":"instance--4f0945c8-f644-50ce-8796-fea52a29dda1","60":"instance--16c43a2d-7356-521d-a507-5922e2c3337b","90":"instance--abce5c62-339a-5ed5-a0b8-dd66136cfe2f"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--4","properties":[["name","Abuse DDE to execute infection chain"],["description","The commands to do this are typically hidden in an attachment, abusing a functionality like Visual Basic, Object Linking or \u2014 as in last week\u2019s example \u2014 Dynamic Data Exchange or DDE."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0002","technique":"T1559.001"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--a469636c-0cb2-50b9-92f9-644c8aa98197","120":"instance--d57b3a21-e910-5879-8148-40165cea451a","150":"instance--58250ef4-5bb4-5bf3-b33e-89493bbb395d","180":"instance--3e769cf2-c1e5-5d2e-81d4-892f48ce4d86","210":"instance--f6499e41-749c-5d7f-9346-96c08d0d5dfd","240":"instance--d9dcdfc8-5f42-546a-803a-0efcd5d4cf91","270":"instance--c9afd0f6-97ce-57b2-9d60-3557b6214809","30":"instance--75f82155-f5ff-5619-8bf8-aae22937cab0","300":"instance--25e2d26e-1b35-56bd-b9aa-096c2d3b0e3c","330":"instance--e0483688-da10-5376-8cf2-050bcc3b70f0","60":"instance--1293d9cc-16b2-5c67-a453-bd144aab133a","90":"instance--2b43cd52-10db-5b15-8ad5-c4b59496528b"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--5","properties":[["name","Inject code into working memory"],["description","Instead, they use tools already installed on the target\u2019s own computers \u2014 powerful and widely trusted system and security programs like or \u2014 to inject their malicious code directly into the computer\u2019s working memory."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0005","technique":"T1055"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--54fc1f38-f4e3-523e-b07c-73889b0d8df7","120":"instance--9cf45948-7040-5d7a-a1d5-3cb4db0c1af6","150":"instance--13bb13cc-e02b-51d2-8d7d-40e5613b6e5a","180":"instance--e33bc6ee-771e-54fe-a772-74dfdaad420d","210":"instance--286f51a3-8fc6-55ec-978e-8b05ebda3655","240":"instance--14659696-be77-5460-beb1-4b5eac126e43","270":"instance--f48ed1a6-2895-5cd2-9b1c-e30ac2bc8921","30":"instance--7b803e61-16ac-5720-92cd-8f2a456a52b7","300":"instance--76c24361-5143-5c43-8e4d-707c619e6038","330":"instance--f395cfc7-395a-5001-9552-a4fec6dbc53a","60":"instance--760885bb-9294-5a5b-93a2-a410e1ea4112","90":"instance--8e0d1a12-8611-598d-9a7d-40f2525e4781"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--6","properties":[["name","Block researcher IP"],["description","Earlier this year, when FIN7 encountered a Morphisec researcher during an incident response, the group first blocked the IP he was using and then abandoned their entire command and control infrastructure."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0005","technique":"T1562"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--7cccbcd0-a724-54fb-be4f-ac523d26f7d0","120":"instance--738e44b2-1357-5eb3-82bd-8a0ce8942b72","150":"instance--d31f4735-6339-5929-8d7c-d30863cf166f","180":"instance--2252393d-d801-5931-ad38-4b53374a9880","210":"instance--065b5ad5-023a-5336-b458-e9c9dcda2976","240":"instance--5ea0dd2b-5eac-51f8-855a-4cbcb801bc2d","270":"instance--bba66874-a069-56c6-bb95-967cb3cefc9e","30":"instance--6377c09d-ecb4-5567-a2f4-4dde56ff4f98","300":"instance--ede3430f-b16b-58ae-be71-1d1f1a194336","330":"instance--7772f482-8ee2-569a-b600-7528c065d4e0","60":"instance--98139a98-16b0-54fe-8c77-3473c1b520cd","90":"instance--5cb9cc95-e190-5a68-985d-0a94d39299e6"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--7","properties":[["name","Abandon command and control infrastructure"],["description","Earlier this year, when FIN7 encountered a Morphisec researcher during an incident response, the group first blocked the IP he was using and then abandoned their entire command and control infrastructure."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0042","technique":"T1584"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--35652c79-2c41-5d60-81ba-b5e47aa554bf","120":"instance--53906203-fffb-5af3-b112-44a9b4b49b8f","150":"instance--465fbc8a-7b4c-569f-be00-c0fbc137fcfc","180":"instance--a653c96b-3673-5dfa-968e-188fffe4cc04","210":"instance--6a344cf5-bd5c-52db-84f5-23c7701c7a5e","30":"instance--913561d1-b5f3-54d2-8272-159233dfde54","330":"instance--d59fe52d-c897-5f3a-919a-c2273cb8a8b3","60":"instance--f1fd6a3d-bb83-543d-a379-39d4632978f7","90":"instance--4cd6fce2-0d24-57f0-b161-12a867cd1100","branch:False":"instance--f7e897b3-3607-5ea5-8d15-5f83ba8a60da","branch:True":"instance--39b5ac19-b0dd-5674-a7d9-d75e659fe9ea"},"id":"condition","instance":"attack-condition--1","properties":[["description","Microsoft users will generally get a pop-up box asking them if they want to \u201cenable content\u201d or \u201cupdate links\u201d in the document they\u2019re opening"]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--20bbe9f2-ac00-5017-9562-e92ae507e48d","120":"instance--2e844599-4e31-5871-a7c7-04a9c6ce5691","150":"instance--af5a54f1-2b8c-545d-ab59-74cfcebc16f4","180":"instance--c5b59f65-1